From: siraisisatoru <37771374+siraisisatoru@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 22:57:17 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] umac_ap: fix STA record use after free on removal

umac_ap_remove_sta_record() frees the STA record while two kinds of
reference to it are still live.

1. The removal notification. mmosal_free(stad) runs before
   umac_ap_notify_sta_status_change(stad, ...). That function only uses
   stad for the relay hook, umac_relay_handle_ap_sta_state(), which
   dereferences it several times:

     - umac_sta_data_get_umacd(stad) to find the relay data,
     - umac_interface_peek_mac_addr(stad), which reads the umacd and VIF
       ID from the record, to get the initiator address,
     - umac_relay_process_reachable_address_update(), which reads the
       peer address from the record as the next hop.

   With relay mode enabled (root or repeater) every station that leaves
   the BSS (deauth, disassociation, inactivity, AP stop) therefore reads
   freed heap memory. Once the block is reused this crashes or corrupts
   the relay table, and in practice the root/repeater faults on the
   first disassociation.

   The AP stop path, umac_ap_stop(), keeps data->stas[ii] pointing at
   the record until the call returns, so dump_sta_list() (built at
   MMLOG_LEVEL_VRB) also walks the freed record.

2. Armed core timeouts. The function tears down only rate control and
   the TX queue. Three timeouts whose arguments are the record, or point
   into it, can still be pending and fire after the free, in any AP mode:

     - umac_ba_addba_req_timeout_handler(stad, &session), armed on TX to
       the station (100 ms backoff doubling to 60 s) and cancelled only
       when an ADDBA response or DELBA arrives; it reads session->status
       and transmits a DELBA through stad,
     - umac_datapath_rx_reorder_timeout_handler(umacd, stad), armed
       whenever an out-of-order MPDU is buffered and never cancelled,
     - datapath_defrag_timeout(frag_chain), with frag_chain embedded in
       the record.

   The mmpkts held in the RX reorder list and the fragment chains are
   also leaked on every removal, which slowly drains the RX pool.

Fix:

  - Free the record as the last step, after the notification and the
    debug dump.
  - Use umac_datapath_stad_flush() instead of
    umac_datapath_stad_flush_txq(). It is what the STA disconnect path
    already uses: it drains the RX reorder list, runs
    datapath_defrag_deinit() (which releases the chains and cancels their
    timeouts) and flushes the TX queue. It now also cancels the RX
    reorder timeout for the record.
  - Call umac_ba_deinit(), which now cancels the ADDBA request timeouts
    of every TID for the record before clearing the BA state.

The STA disconnect path calls the same two functions, so it also stops
leaving stale reorder and ADDBA timeouts behind; its record is never
freed, so for it this is only tidier.
---
 framework/morselib/src/umac/ap/umac_ap.c             | 12 +++++++++---
 framework/morselib/src/umac/ba/umac_ba.c             |  7 +++++++
 framework/morselib/src/umac/datapath/umac_datapath.c |  1 +
 3 files changed, 17 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/framework/morselib/src/umac/ap/umac_ap.c b/framework/morselib/src/umac/ap/umac_ap.c
index 6541aa8..9cd6898 100644
--- a/framework/morselib/src/umac/ap/umac_ap.c
+++ b/framework/morselib/src/umac/ap/umac_ap.c
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
 #include "dot11/dot11_utils.h"
 
 #include "umac_ap.h"
+#include "umac/ba/umac_ba.h"
 #include "umac/core/umac_core.h"
 #include "umac/stats/umac_stats.h"
 #include "umac_ap_data.h"
@@ -947,11 +948,12 @@ static enum mmwlan_status umac_ap_remove_sta_record(struct umac_data *umacd,
 
     umac_rc_stop(stad);
     umac_rc_deinit(stad);
-    umac_datapath_stad_flush_txq(umacd, stad);
+    /* Release the RX reorder list, fragment chains and TX queue and cancel the core timeouts
+     * (RX reorder, defrag, ADDBA request) that point into this record before it is freed. */
+    umac_datapath_stad_flush(umacd, stad);
+    umac_ba_deinit(stad);
     ap_traffic_bitmap_clear_aid_bit(data->bitmap, aid);
 
-    mmosal_free(stad);
-
     if (update_required)
     {
         MMLOG_VRB("Invoke STA callback (remove)\n");
@@ -962,6 +964,10 @@ static enum mmwlan_status umac_ap_remove_sta_record(struct umac_data *umacd,
     dump_sta_list(data);
 #endif
 
+    /* Must be last: the notification above (relay handler) and, on the AP stop path where
+     * data->stas[aid] still references this record, dump_sta_list() both dereference stad. */
+    mmosal_free(stad);
+
     return status;
 }
 
diff --git a/framework/morselib/src/umac/ba/umac_ba.c b/framework/morselib/src/umac/ba/umac_ba.c
index 614513e..e3a2d88 100644
--- a/framework/morselib/src/umac/ba/umac_ba.c
+++ b/framework/morselib/src/umac/ba/umac_ba.c
@@ -15,9 +15,16 @@
 #include "umac/datapath/umac_datapath.h"
 #include "umac/core/umac_core.h"
 
+static void umac_ba_addba_req_timeout_handler(void *arg1, void *arg2);
+
 void umac_ba_deinit(struct umac_sta_data *stad)
 {
     struct umac_ba_sta_data *data = umac_sta_data_get_ba(stad);
+    /* The ADDBA request timeout points at the session inside this record (one per TID). */
+    (void)umac_core_cancel_timeout(umac_sta_data_get_umacd(stad),
+                                   umac_ba_addba_req_timeout_handler,
+                                   stad,
+                                   UMAC_CORE_TIMEOUT_ANY_CTX);
     memset(data, 0, sizeof(*data));
 }
 
diff --git a/framework/morselib/src/umac/datapath/umac_datapath.c b/framework/morselib/src/umac/datapath/umac_datapath.c
index 576969d..c0b2940 100644
--- a/framework/morselib/src/umac/datapath/umac_datapath.c
+++ b/framework/morselib/src/umac/datapath/umac_datapath.c
@@ -1217,6 +1217,7 @@ void umac_datapath_stad_flush(struct umac_data *umacd, struct umac_sta_data *sta
     MMOSAL_ASSERT(stad != NULL);
     struct umac_datapath_sta_data *sta_data = umac_sta_data_get_datapath(stad);
     umac_datapath_flush_rx_reorder_list(stad, sta_data);
+    (void)umac_core_cancel_timeout(umacd, umac_datapath_rx_reorder_timeout_handler, umacd, stad);
     datapath_defrag_deinit(umacd, &sta_data->defrag_data);
     umac_datapath_stad_flush_txq(umacd, stad);
 }
